1
00:00:42,355 --> 00:00:46,067
‎SPOOKY IN LOVE

2
00:02:21,287 --> 00:02:23,498
‎EPISODE 3

3
00:02:52,235 --> 00:02:53,903
‎How dare you blackmail me?

4
00:02:53,987 --> 00:02:57,740
‎I didn't make a fuss
‎when you copied my designs last season.

5
00:02:57,824 --> 00:03:00,326
‎But I didn't think you'd copy
‎my ‎haenyeo‎ diver dress.

6
00:03:01,619 --> 00:03:04,497
‎It was a special dress I made
‎while thinking of my grandmother.

7
00:03:06,082 --> 00:03:06,916
‎Hey, listen.

8
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:10,545
‎Why would I copy the design
‎of a lowly nobody like you?

9
00:03:10,628 --> 00:03:12,880
‎You can run your mouth all you want,

10
00:03:12,964 --> 00:03:14,549
‎but who would believe you?

11
00:03:16,426 --> 00:03:18,803
‎Wait and find out if they believe me.

12
00:03:19,387 --> 00:03:21,889
‎Circumstantial evidence
‎that you copied my designs

13
00:03:22,598 --> 00:03:24,726
‎was caught on the surveillance cameras.

14
00:03:32,400 --> 00:03:34,485
‎You came well-prepared, didn't you?

15
00:03:35,528 --> 00:03:37,238
‎Give me that phone.

16
00:03:41,409 --> 00:03:42,577
‎Put my name on the design.

17
00:03:42,660 --> 00:03:44,245
‎Give me the phone!

18
00:03:44,329 --> 00:03:47,248
‎-Say you used my designs!
‎-Give me the damn phone!

19
00:04:09,395 --> 00:04:10,521
‎Da-mi!

20
00:06:00,756 --> 00:06:01,924
‎Don't you have something to say?

21
00:06:04,719 --> 00:06:06,179
‎What do you mean?

22
00:06:07,263 --> 00:06:08,556
‎It wasn't a coincidence, was it?

23
00:06:10,683 --> 00:06:12,685
‎The mountain where we first met,

24
00:06:12,768 --> 00:06:16,022
‎the taxi driver's body in the trunk,
‎and now, Jang Eun-ju.

25
00:06:17,106 --> 00:06:19,692
‎It's a huge stretch,
‎but let's say that was all a coincidence.

26
00:06:19,775 --> 00:06:21,235
‎But for this to be by chance too?

27
00:06:24,405 --> 00:06:26,115
‎What is it you want to say?

28
00:06:26,199 --> 00:06:27,533
‎If it were you…

29
00:06:34,165 --> 00:06:35,666
‎Let's talk about it another time.

30
00:06:36,584 --> 00:06:38,336
‎You should go inside and warm up.

31
00:06:45,009 --> 00:06:45,927
‎About earlier…

32
00:06:50,389 --> 00:06:51,390
‎Thank you.

33
00:06:55,603 --> 00:06:57,355
‎I might be used to how things are,

34
00:06:58,981 --> 00:07:00,775
‎but that doesn't mean I'm not afraid.

35
00:07:07,573 --> 00:07:09,033
‎Please take care of this for me.

36
00:07:10,785 --> 00:07:13,663
‎You'd be better at handling it than me.

37
00:07:33,349 --> 00:07:35,685
‎I swear, it was a setup.

38
00:07:35,768 --> 00:07:37,436
‎There must be a mistake!

39
00:07:37,520 --> 00:07:40,982
‎-Don't take any photos.
‎-It's all just a misunderstanding!

40
00:07:41,065 --> 00:07:43,067
‎-Don't take photos.
‎-Ms. Kim!

41
00:07:43,150 --> 00:07:44,318
‎-Ms. Jung!
‎-Can you prove it was…

42
00:07:44,819 --> 00:07:45,778
‎-Ms. Kim.
‎-Yes?

43
00:07:45,861 --> 00:07:47,655
‎Find out whoever did this.

44
00:07:47,738 --> 00:07:49,407
‎-I'll demand reparation.
‎-Yes, ma'am.

45
00:07:49,490 --> 00:07:50,491
‎Be gentle with her.

46
00:07:58,874 --> 00:08:00,918
‎Come on out. Watch your step.

47
00:08:01,961 --> 00:08:04,964
‎-Thank you. Please watch your step.
‎-Grandma?

48
00:08:05,840 --> 00:08:07,675
‎This is where you'll be staying.

49
00:08:07,758 --> 00:08:11,721
‎You'll rest in the lobby for a while,
‎and then we'll hand out the keys.

50
00:08:11,804 --> 00:08:13,598
‎We'll show you where to go then.

51
00:08:14,974 --> 00:08:16,684
‎-Shall we?
‎-Hey.

52
00:08:16,767 --> 00:08:17,977
‎Grandma, are you in Jeju Island?

53
00:08:18,060 --> 00:08:21,105
‎Why would I be there? I'm at the temple.

54
00:08:21,188 --> 00:08:22,898
‎-Are you in Jeju Island?
‎-Yeah.

55
00:08:23,649 --> 00:08:25,276
‎Are you sure you're not here?

56
00:08:25,359 --> 00:08:27,403
‎What nonsense are you on about?

57
00:08:27,486 --> 00:08:31,365
‎By the way, you must stay away
‎from large bodies of water today.

58
00:08:31,449 --> 00:08:32,325
‎Okay.

59
00:08:35,369 --> 00:08:38,122
‎Man, is she psychic or something?

60
00:08:41,083 --> 00:08:42,543
‎Did you reach the airport safely?

61
00:08:42,627 --> 00:08:44,712
‎Yeah, I'm almost there.

62
00:08:45,296 --> 00:08:46,881
‎You didn't have to send a car.

63
00:08:46,964 --> 00:08:48,257
‎I heard about the unfortunate accident.

64
00:08:49,050 --> 00:08:51,260
‎I'll let you buy me a meal
‎if you're that grateful.

65
00:08:53,304 --> 00:08:54,555
‎Sure.

66
00:08:54,639 --> 00:08:57,099
‎I'll be going to Seoul soon,
‎so don't forget.

67
00:09:06,192 --> 00:09:08,861
‎Why are you doing that yourself
‎when we have gardeners?

68
00:09:11,697 --> 00:09:12,698
‎I heard about the nuisance.

69
00:09:12,782 --> 00:09:14,784
‎Oh, it's been taken care of.

70
00:09:15,868 --> 00:09:18,996
‎By the way,
‎did you have a visitor earlier?

71
00:09:24,960 --> 00:09:26,587
‎They grow so quickly.

72
00:09:26,671 --> 00:09:31,050
‎If you don't pluck them in time,
‎the weeds will take over the whole garden.

73
00:09:36,681 --> 00:09:37,515
‎Hey.

74
00:09:37,598 --> 00:09:41,018
‎You should stay with her
‎until Da-mi is moved to the burial site.

75
00:09:42,728 --> 00:09:46,399
‎We can't both miss work,
‎so I had to come back.

76
00:09:49,527 --> 00:09:51,070
‎But it just breaks my heart.

77
00:09:51,654 --> 00:09:52,655
‎Okay, bye.

78
00:10:11,590 --> 00:10:14,468
‎I was definitely within arm's reach,

79
00:10:15,761 --> 00:10:18,556
‎but I get the feeling
‎she deliberately avoided grabbing me.

80
00:10:19,181 --> 00:10:21,726
‎About earlier… Thank you.

81
00:10:22,727 --> 00:10:24,729
‎I might be used to how things are,

82
00:10:25,438 --> 00:10:27,523
‎but that doesn't mean I'm not afraid.

83
00:10:30,025 --> 00:10:31,402
‎What was she thanking me for?

84
00:10:32,987 --> 00:10:34,155
‎She's a strange one.

85
00:10:57,011 --> 00:10:58,763
‎I heard you rejected Min-hwan's offer.

86
00:10:59,805 --> 00:11:00,639
‎Yes.

87
00:11:01,265 --> 00:11:04,435
‎I'll flesh out the strategy
‎I showed you last time.

88
00:11:04,518 --> 00:11:06,812
‎Review it for me again.
‎I'm confident I can manage.

89
00:11:07,521 --> 00:11:09,231
‎How did it feel to see him again?

90
00:11:09,315 --> 00:11:10,316
‎Well…

91
00:11:13,152 --> 00:11:15,905
‎Did you send me to Jeju Island
‎because of Min-hwan?

92
00:11:15,988 --> 00:11:18,324
‎Yes, and since we're on the topic…

93
00:11:18,407 --> 00:11:20,826
‎I quite like him. What about you?

94
00:11:22,369 --> 00:11:24,413
‎You mean, romantically?

95
00:11:25,164 --> 00:11:27,750
‎He's just a friend I went to school with.

96
00:11:27,833 --> 00:11:29,502
‎I told you last time, didn't I?

97
00:11:29,585 --> 00:11:32,546
‎To squash the rumor
‎that's going on about you,

98
00:11:33,380 --> 00:11:35,007
‎marriage is the best option.

99
00:11:35,090 --> 00:11:36,926
‎-Grandma.
‎-We can't have such rumors.

100
00:11:38,010 --> 00:11:40,596
‎It's not just about the hotel.
‎What about our family's reputation?

101
00:11:41,347 --> 00:11:43,641
‎Dispel the rumor yourself,
‎with a marriage.

102
00:11:44,433 --> 00:11:46,894
‎Come on, this isn't the Joseon Dynasty.

103
00:11:46,977 --> 00:11:50,022
‎You can't force me to get married.

104
00:11:50,105 --> 00:11:51,148
‎Your marriage

105
00:11:52,399 --> 00:11:53,776
‎isn't just any union.

106
00:11:54,818 --> 00:11:57,530
‎What if the line of succession
‎passes to Dong-jun and Ha-ri?

107
00:11:58,447 --> 00:12:01,909
‎There is the disadvantage
‎that their father isn't my biological son,

108
00:12:01,992 --> 00:12:03,244
‎but you know that

109
00:12:03,327 --> 00:12:06,288
‎when it comes to succession,
‎it's not just about blood.

110
00:12:07,540 --> 00:12:10,751
‎With Min-hwan's help,
‎you could sign with a foreign hotel chain,

111
00:12:10,834 --> 00:12:12,920
‎and naturally get together in the process…

112
00:12:13,003 --> 00:12:14,588
‎I have no intention of doing that.

113
00:12:14,672 --> 00:12:15,673
‎And I

114
00:12:16,173 --> 00:12:17,550
‎don't plan to wait for long.

115
00:12:18,759 --> 00:12:19,969
‎This is the right time

116
00:12:20,052 --> 00:12:23,681
‎to clear up the rumors
‎that are going around about you.

117
00:12:23,764 --> 00:12:25,641
‎Get married within two months.

118
00:12:26,350 --> 00:12:27,518
‎If you don't,

119
00:12:27,601 --> 00:12:30,187
‎I'll bring the Reina licensing talk
‎back to the table.

120
00:12:31,021 --> 00:12:32,231
‎And Siena Hall too.

121
00:12:36,235 --> 00:12:37,945
‎Well, at least

122
00:12:38,028 --> 00:12:39,863
‎make it an engagement for now.

123
00:12:39,947 --> 00:12:41,991
‎Since it was my engagement ceremony
‎that fell through.

124
00:12:42,074 --> 00:12:44,285
‎The deadline remains the same. Two months.

125
00:12:45,661 --> 00:12:48,289
‎On that note, I'd be happy with Min-hwan.

126
00:12:49,456 --> 00:12:52,001
‎But like you said,
‎this isn't the Joseon Dynasty.

127
00:12:54,545 --> 00:12:59,174
‎Still, he should at least
‎measure up to our family.

128
00:12:59,258 --> 00:13:01,802
‎Okay. Let's get back to it.

129
00:13:19,153 --> 00:13:20,362
‎Go on ahead.

130
00:13:24,116 --> 00:13:27,995
‎Now, you're putting Seung-jae behind you

131
00:13:28,078 --> 00:13:29,830
‎and getting out there
‎on blind dates, okay?

132
00:13:35,210 --> 00:13:37,504
‎We bought everything you wanted.

133
00:13:40,132 --> 00:13:41,175
‎Okay.

134
00:13:42,760 --> 00:13:45,512
‎Does Grandma have no interest
‎in opening a department store?

135
00:13:45,596 --> 00:13:46,597
‎Reina Department Store.

136
00:13:47,264 --> 00:13:49,141
‎I'm sure I'd do a good job running it.

137
00:13:50,309 --> 00:13:52,895
‎It's hard enough to get her
‎to give us another art gallery.

138
00:13:53,395 --> 00:13:55,022
‎Forget about a department store.

139
00:13:56,065 --> 00:13:57,775
‎Yeo-ri hasn't caught on yet, right?

140
00:13:58,275 --> 00:13:59,318
‎About the hotel artworks.

141
00:14:02,029 --> 00:14:02,905
‎Cheon Ha-ri?

142
00:14:04,573 --> 00:14:06,033
‎Is that you, Min-hwan?

143
00:14:06,116 --> 00:14:07,618
‎Wow, how long has it been?

144
00:14:07,701 --> 00:14:10,996
‎Oh, my goodness. Look who it is.

145
00:14:11,080 --> 00:14:12,164
‎How have you been?

146
00:14:12,247 --> 00:14:13,540
‎I've been very well.

147
00:14:13,624 --> 00:14:14,792
‎When did you come back to Korea?

148
00:14:15,584 --> 00:14:17,127
‎Well, not too long ago.

149
00:14:17,711 --> 00:14:19,672
‎We haven't met in a while.
‎How about we eat together?

150
00:14:22,800 --> 00:14:25,010
‎I'm here to buy a gift, so I can't today.

151
00:14:25,094 --> 00:14:26,845
‎I'll treat you to something nice soon.

152
00:14:27,596 --> 00:14:28,514
‎You too, Ms. Ok.

153
00:14:36,563 --> 00:14:37,606
‎Come in.

154
00:14:41,610 --> 00:14:42,528
‎Chairwoman Baek.

155
00:14:42,611 --> 00:14:43,529
‎Min-hwan.

156
00:14:47,324 --> 00:14:48,659
‎It's been so long.

157
00:14:50,953 --> 00:14:52,287
‎Min-hwan.

158
00:14:53,080 --> 00:14:54,498
‎-This is for you.
‎-Goodness.

159
00:14:54,999 --> 00:14:56,250
‎Oh, gosh.

160
00:14:56,792 --> 00:14:57,751
‎It's beautiful.

161
00:14:58,752 --> 00:15:00,796
‎You didn't have to get me anything.

162
00:15:01,338 --> 00:15:03,841
‎It's so nice to see you in person
‎after just some phone calls.

163
00:15:03,924 --> 00:15:05,634
‎-It really is.
‎-Let's sit down.

164
00:15:07,094 --> 00:15:10,305
‎You haven't changed at all.
‎You look even more radiant.

165
00:15:10,389 --> 00:15:12,266
‎Oh, don't you tease an old woman.

166
00:15:15,394 --> 00:15:19,023
‎I heard you and Yeo-ri
‎didn't reach an agreement.

167
00:15:20,441 --> 00:15:22,317
‎You sent her over knowing
‎how it would turn out.

168
00:15:23,027 --> 00:15:24,820
‎I appreciate the cooperation.

169
00:15:26,280 --> 00:15:27,114
‎Goodness.

170
00:15:27,865 --> 00:15:29,199
‎Should we have dinner with Yeo-ri?

171
00:15:30,284 --> 00:15:31,368
‎I'd love to.

172
00:15:31,452 --> 00:15:33,245
‎What was it that you liked to eat?

173
00:15:34,204 --> 00:15:35,497
‎Anything you like?

174
00:15:38,083 --> 00:15:39,543
‎I don't really mind it much.

175
00:15:40,044 --> 00:15:41,295
‎Hello, ma'am.

176
00:15:42,046 --> 00:15:43,297
‎Ms. Cheon's in, right?

177
00:15:44,256 --> 00:15:46,341
‎She just left to go home.

178
00:15:46,425 --> 00:15:47,801
‎Should I give her a call?

179
00:15:47,885 --> 00:15:49,386
‎No need.

180
00:15:49,470 --> 00:15:51,388
‎She doesn't even take my calls after work.

181
00:15:52,848 --> 00:15:54,391
‎I've spoiled her.

182
00:15:55,809 --> 00:15:56,685
‎That's too bad.

183
00:15:56,769 --> 00:16:00,064
‎We'll have to eat together
‎some other time.

184
00:16:00,147 --> 00:16:02,357
‎No. I like this even better.

185
00:16:02,441 --> 00:16:03,650
‎We can spend some quality time.

186
00:16:03,734 --> 00:16:04,818
‎Right?

187
00:16:04,902 --> 00:16:06,779
‎Let's just relax and eat something nice.

188
00:16:06,862 --> 00:16:07,696
‎Sounds good.

189
00:16:30,594 --> 00:16:32,763
‎Min-hwan and Ji-hwan aren't twins?

190
00:16:32,846 --> 00:16:35,099
‎Keep your voice down.

191
00:16:35,182 --> 00:16:36,725
‎My sister will kill me if she hears you.

192
00:16:39,186 --> 00:16:42,314
‎The truth is, after my sister
‎learned she was infertile,

193
00:16:42,940 --> 00:16:45,067
‎she adopted a baby from the US.

194
00:16:45,567 --> 00:16:47,736
‎But right before she returned to Korea,

195
00:16:47,820 --> 00:16:49,947
‎-she miraculously got pregnant.
‎-Oh, gosh.

196
00:16:50,030 --> 00:16:51,990
‎That's why she delayed her return

197
00:16:52,074 --> 00:16:54,409
‎and came back
‎after giving birth to Ji-hwan.

198
00:16:54,952 --> 00:16:56,495
‎I wondered why she stayed abroad so long.

199
00:16:56,578 --> 00:16:59,790
‎So Min-hwan was adopted, after all.

200
00:16:59,873 --> 00:17:01,959
‎-Exactly.
‎-No wonder…

201
00:17:15,055 --> 00:17:18,725
‎Could that be why they want to
‎send Min-hwan abroad to study?

202
00:17:21,061 --> 00:17:22,437
‎What are you doing over there?

203
00:17:23,355 --> 00:17:24,398
‎Yeo-ri, you're here too.

204
00:17:24,481 --> 00:17:26,733
‎-Join us for some fruit.
‎-No, thank you.

205
00:17:26,817 --> 00:17:29,444
‎We were on our way out.

206
00:17:29,528 --> 00:17:30,445
‎Were you?

207
00:17:32,281 --> 00:17:33,157
‎Let's go.

208
00:17:43,959 --> 00:17:45,085
‎What do you want?

209
00:17:45,169 --> 00:17:47,004
‎We agreed to a bet.

210
00:17:48,672 --> 00:17:49,590
‎Can't it wait?

211
00:17:49,673 --> 00:17:53,093
‎No way. A promise is a promise.

212
00:17:53,802 --> 00:17:55,179
‎Keep your word.

213
00:18:04,813 --> 00:18:05,981
‎If I win,

214
00:18:07,024 --> 00:18:08,734
‎give me the game console
‎you bought yesterday.

215
00:18:13,071 --> 00:18:14,990
‎That's not fair. It's mine.

216
00:18:15,616 --> 00:18:17,075
‎Then beat me.

217
00:19:01,453 --> 00:19:02,663
‎Hey, Gang-uk!

218
00:19:02,746 --> 00:19:04,289
‎-I think I forgot something.
‎-Gang-uk.

219
00:19:04,373 --> 00:19:05,832
‎-What?
‎-I got the office next to yours.

220
00:19:05,916 --> 00:19:07,292
‎Then we're just neighbors.

221
00:19:07,376 --> 00:19:08,835
‎We have a connection, don't we?

222
00:19:08,919 --> 00:19:10,796
‎-Will you please…
‎-Here.

223
00:19:11,630 --> 00:19:12,464
‎Thank you.

224
00:19:13,632 --> 00:19:14,633
‎How long has it been?

225
00:19:14,716 --> 00:19:17,010
‎What do you mean?
‎We met at Do-jun's wedding.

226
00:19:17,094 --> 00:19:19,221
‎That's a really long time for us.

227
00:19:19,304 --> 00:19:21,974
‎-Jeez, you still yap too much.
‎-Isn't that Prosecutor Im Seo-hyeon

228
00:19:22,057 --> 00:19:23,892
‎from the Ministry of Justice's
‎Criminal Affairs Division?

229
00:19:23,976 --> 00:19:25,602
‎What's going on? Do they know each other?

230
00:19:25,686 --> 00:19:27,187
‎They don't just know each other.

231
00:19:28,188 --> 00:19:30,649
‎What do you mean? Did they date?

232
00:19:30,732 --> 00:19:33,068
‎I wouldn't say they dated.

233
00:19:33,151 --> 00:19:35,654
‎Ever since
‎they went to the same university,

234
00:19:35,737 --> 00:19:39,324
‎their relationship has been like
‎that of the Earth and the moon.

235
00:19:39,408 --> 00:19:40,367
‎The Earth and the moon?

236
00:19:40,450 --> 00:19:44,204
‎-Earth's gravity pulls the moon, right?
‎-Right.

237
00:19:45,247 --> 00:19:49,042
‎Im pulls Ma close with all her might,

238
00:19:49,126 --> 00:19:54,089
‎but Ma spins around her
‎without ever getting too close.

239
00:19:55,382 --> 00:19:56,216
‎It's quite strange.

240
00:19:56,300 --> 00:19:59,303
‎Whenever Ma is
‎transferred somewhere for work,

241
00:19:59,386 --> 00:20:01,888
‎Im also gets herself transferred there.

242
00:20:01,972 --> 00:20:05,851
‎And when Ma transfers somewhere else,
‎Im follows him there too.

243
00:20:06,435 --> 00:20:08,729
‎Does she have connections
‎with the higher-ups?

244
00:20:08,812 --> 00:20:10,063
‎That's what I don't get.

245
00:20:11,606 --> 00:20:12,816
‎It's fascinating.

246
00:20:12,899 --> 00:20:14,192
‎The Earth and the moon…

247
00:20:16,862 --> 00:20:17,696
‎Yes?

248
00:20:19,698 --> 00:20:20,532
‎Hello.

249
00:20:20,615 --> 00:20:22,409
‎It's Mr. Kang, the CEO.

250
00:20:23,368 --> 00:20:25,370
‎-Welcome.
‎-Thank you.

251
00:20:26,538 --> 00:20:28,457
‎I didn't expect to get a call from you.

252
00:20:28,540 --> 00:20:32,044
‎I felt bad that we didn't get to talk
‎after meeting at the department store.

253
00:20:32,127 --> 00:20:33,920
‎It's been so long since we met,

254
00:20:34,004 --> 00:20:36,673
‎and I wanted to treat you to a meal.

255
00:20:36,757 --> 00:20:38,383
‎Was the drive here all right?

256
00:20:38,467 --> 00:20:40,761
‎-Yes, it was fine.
‎-Was it?

257
00:20:42,929 --> 00:20:45,223
‎The thing is, I heard somewhere

258
00:20:45,307 --> 00:20:50,312
‎that G1A Group is trying to sell
‎Fiel Seoul to another company.

259
00:20:50,395 --> 00:20:51,772
‎CL Group has decided to join

260
00:20:51,855 --> 00:20:54,232
‎the bidding war to acquire it, right?

261
00:20:54,316 --> 00:20:57,402
‎Well, we haven't
‎made our position official yet.

262
00:20:58,111 --> 00:20:59,821
‎Your sources are pretty quick.

263
00:21:02,032 --> 00:21:04,242
‎They say some things are open secrets,

264
00:21:04,326 --> 00:21:07,287
‎but to be honest,
‎those in the business know everything.

265
00:21:08,080 --> 00:21:10,123
‎Anyway, I heard you spearheaded

266
00:21:11,083 --> 00:21:12,626
‎the Fiel Seoul acquisition.

267
00:21:12,709 --> 00:21:14,002
‎Well, yes.

268
00:21:14,086 --> 00:21:16,546
‎If you manage to buy Fiel Seoul,

269
00:21:16,630 --> 00:21:19,132
‎will that cement your position
‎as the successor?

270
00:21:20,634 --> 00:21:23,178
‎I'm so impressed, Mr. Kang.

271
00:21:24,971 --> 00:21:27,099
‎So why did you want to see me today?

272
00:21:27,182 --> 00:21:29,017
‎Oh, well…

273
00:21:29,101 --> 00:21:30,227
‎From what I heard,

274
00:21:31,311 --> 00:21:33,939
‎you'll need a great sum of money
‎to win the bid.

275
00:21:34,022 --> 00:21:35,732
‎Do you have the necessary funds?

276
00:21:36,483 --> 00:21:39,736
‎I'm aware that they have a massive debt.

277
00:21:39,820 --> 00:21:42,572
‎If you happen to be
‎in need of more funds,

278
00:21:43,156 --> 00:21:45,367
‎our Reina Resort could offer

279
00:21:45,450 --> 00:21:47,661
‎a partial investment in your project.

280
00:21:49,704 --> 00:21:52,374
‎I appreciate it,
‎but we have our own financial company.

281
00:21:52,457 --> 00:21:54,042
‎Not to mention that this acquisition

282
00:21:54,709 --> 00:21:58,422
‎was my father's long-held ambition,
‎so I have his full support.

283
00:21:58,505 --> 00:22:00,799
‎Oh, yes. I'm sure you do.

284
00:22:00,882 --> 00:22:04,219
‎Right, Chairman Kang
‎and his long-held ambition.

285
00:22:04,302 --> 00:22:07,597
‎Let's work together
‎on another project some other time.

286
00:22:08,181 --> 00:22:09,141
‎Sure.

287
00:22:09,224 --> 00:22:11,518
‎Yes, I would love that.

288
00:22:13,854 --> 00:22:15,814
‎Gosh, my silly daughter Ha-ri.

289
00:22:16,440 --> 00:22:20,026
‎She never stopped talking about you,

290
00:22:20,110 --> 00:22:23,530
‎but I can't reach her today
‎and I don't know where she went.

291
00:22:27,784 --> 00:22:28,785
‎Hey, Ha-ri.

292
00:22:30,245 --> 00:22:31,163
‎Take a seat.

293
00:22:35,876 --> 00:22:38,461
‎This is the last time I'm visiting
‎out of loyalty as your ex.

294
00:22:38,545 --> 00:22:41,590
‎Ha-ri, I think
‎I'll be out of here pretty soon.

295
00:22:41,673 --> 00:22:43,216
‎That's impossible.

296
00:22:43,300 --> 00:22:45,051
‎You can't get out
‎when they found her body.

297
00:22:45,135 --> 00:22:47,179
‎It's just not official yet.

298
00:22:48,054 --> 00:22:50,515
‎Let's patch things up when I get out.

299
00:22:50,599 --> 00:22:52,017
‎Patch what up?

300
00:22:52,100 --> 00:22:55,478
‎You ruined our company's
‎entire reputation.

301
00:22:56,021 --> 00:22:59,900
‎Ha-ri, nothing's easier to manipulate
‎than public opinion.

302
00:22:59,983 --> 00:23:01,902
‎My dad's already working on it.

303
00:23:01,985 --> 00:23:04,112
‎That woman was a gold-digger
‎with a dirty past.

304
00:23:04,196 --> 00:23:06,156
‎She used me from start to finish.

305
00:23:09,159 --> 00:23:11,036
‎I believe you.

306
00:23:11,119 --> 00:23:12,954
‎But my mom's turned her back on you.

307
00:23:13,455 --> 00:23:16,791
‎The engagement's off,
‎and I'm supposed to cut you off.

308
00:23:18,501 --> 00:23:19,336
‎Ha-ri.

309
00:23:19,836 --> 00:23:22,839
‎The heart follows where the money is.

310
00:23:22,923 --> 00:23:26,051
‎My dad's still going strong.
‎He has all the power I need.

311
00:23:28,511 --> 00:23:29,971
‎As soon as I get out,

312
00:23:30,597 --> 00:23:31,890
‎I swear on my life

313
00:23:32,933 --> 00:23:34,684
‎that I'll help you take over Reina.

314
00:23:53,245 --> 00:23:54,955
‎Why? What do you want?

315
00:23:55,038 --> 00:23:57,165
‎I just can't seem to make sense of it.

316
00:23:58,792 --> 00:24:00,669
‎How did you know where to go?

317
00:24:01,253 --> 00:24:04,547
‎You just happened to be there
‎and found a body in the water tank,

318
00:24:05,298 --> 00:24:06,591
‎and the prosecutor showed up too?

319
00:24:09,678 --> 00:24:11,596
‎About the weird rumors
‎going around about you…

320
00:24:15,141 --> 00:24:17,227
‎Do you still see ghosts or something?

321
00:24:21,564 --> 00:24:22,524
‎You do, don't you?

322
00:24:25,026 --> 00:24:26,653
‎You always go

323
00:24:27,862 --> 00:24:29,698
‎a bit too far.

324
00:24:29,781 --> 00:24:32,826
‎I can't let a possessed shaman
‎take over Reina.

325
00:24:33,952 --> 00:24:35,328
‎If I reveal the truth about that,

326
00:24:35,954 --> 00:24:38,290
‎Grandma will give up the idea
‎of letting you take over.

327
00:24:40,750 --> 00:24:42,377
‎If that's all you have to say,
‎I'm leaving.

328
00:25:21,666 --> 00:25:24,961
‎You that inhabit the body of this woman!

329
00:25:25,628 --> 00:25:27,756
‎You evil spirit!

330
00:25:28,548 --> 00:25:30,467
‎Begone!

331
00:25:34,888 --> 00:25:35,764
‎Yeo-ri?

332
00:25:37,932 --> 00:25:38,767
‎Yeo-ri.

333
00:25:41,853 --> 00:25:43,188
‎Grandma.

334
00:25:43,271 --> 00:25:44,647
‎Well done.

335
00:25:45,690 --> 00:25:47,025
‎You held up well.

336
00:25:47,901 --> 00:25:51,529
‎Shaman Baek said he suppressed the evil.

337
00:25:51,613 --> 00:25:52,614
‎How do you feel?

338
00:25:54,240 --> 00:25:56,493
‎Do you still see things?

339
00:26:06,669 --> 00:26:07,629
‎I don't…

340
00:26:10,673 --> 00:26:12,133
‎anymore.

341
00:26:15,095 --> 00:26:16,805
‎I guess they're gone.

342
00:26:48,378 --> 00:26:49,504
‎Do it again.

343
00:26:49,587 --> 00:26:51,423
‎-Again?
‎-Do it again.

344
00:26:58,012 --> 00:26:59,889
‎A hotel is not a facility!

345
00:26:59,973 --> 00:27:02,100
‎-It's where memories are made.
‎-It's where memories are made.

346
00:27:02,183 --> 00:27:04,686
‎-Let's go, Reina!
‎-Let's go!

347
00:27:04,769 --> 00:27:07,564
‎-Enjoy yourselves, everyone.
‎-Let's drink.

348
00:27:43,099 --> 00:27:45,351
‎You want me to step down
‎when I indicted him?

349
00:27:45,435 --> 00:27:46,478
‎That makes no sense.

350
00:27:46,561 --> 00:27:50,023
‎Didn't I tell you to give in
‎when you had the chance?

351
00:27:50,106 --> 00:27:52,692
‎Even so. You should've shielded me.

352
00:27:53,568 --> 00:27:54,861
‎Don't you know how we work?

353
00:27:55,445 --> 00:27:57,489
‎We do whatever the higher-ups tell us.

354
00:27:57,572 --> 00:28:00,074
‎What if I were to get caught
‎in the backlash?

355
00:28:00,158 --> 00:28:02,368
‎I must survive if I'm to help you out.

356
00:28:04,454 --> 00:28:06,206
‎I have to say, Assemblyman Park

357
00:28:06,289 --> 00:28:07,999
‎has still got some fight left in him.

358
00:28:09,417 --> 00:28:12,128
‎Even after what his son did,
‎he managed to fight back hard.

359
00:28:13,546 --> 00:28:15,423
‎TRANSFER NOTICE
‎CRIMINAL PROSECUTION 12, MA GANG-UK

360
00:28:15,507 --> 00:28:17,217
‎PROSECUTOR MA GANG-UK TO COLD CASE UNIT

361
00:28:17,300 --> 00:28:20,762
‎We had already decided to beef up
‎Criminal Prosecution

362
00:28:21,387 --> 00:28:24,307
‎and revamp the Cold Case Unit anyway.

363
00:28:25,099 --> 00:28:27,310
‎Solve some cases while you're over there.

364
00:28:29,687 --> 00:28:30,605
‎I'll bring you back
‎when the time is right.

365
00:28:39,614 --> 00:28:42,116
‎Don't you think things are going backward?

366
00:28:42,200 --> 00:28:44,160
‎Why am I getting demoted
‎for solving a case?

367
00:28:44,244 --> 00:28:46,996
‎Accept it and go with the flow.
‎It's not like this is anything new.

368
00:28:47,080 --> 00:28:49,582
‎Fine. You wait and see.

369
00:28:49,666 --> 00:28:51,626
‎Let's see what you say
‎if this happens to you.

370
00:28:51,709 --> 00:28:54,921
‎Just go, "Oh, I guess this is it then."

371
00:28:55,004 --> 00:28:57,090
‎"This is just how things are."

372
00:28:57,173 --> 00:29:00,385
‎If you take everything to heart,
‎you'll end up dying young.

373
00:29:00,468 --> 00:29:02,136
‎-Aren't I right?
‎-You are.

374
00:29:02,637 --> 00:29:04,848
‎I'm not even surprised, you know.

375
00:29:04,931 --> 00:29:07,225
‎Why are you more immature
‎than your junior?

376
00:29:07,308 --> 00:29:10,186
‎Why do you keep yawning?
‎Did you not sleep well?

377
00:29:10,270 --> 00:29:11,855
‎It's not that.

378
00:29:12,438 --> 00:29:16,025
‎I just had a really stressful dream
‎that felt so real.

379
00:29:16,109 --> 00:29:17,485
‎In the dream,

380
00:29:18,736 --> 00:29:23,032
‎I was going somewhere when something
‎suddenly appeared in front of me.

381
00:29:23,658 --> 00:29:24,909
‎It was my late grandmother.

382
00:29:24,993 --> 00:29:27,203
‎-Okay.
‎-I asked her what was up.

383
00:29:27,287 --> 00:29:29,581
‎She just stared at me,
‎then all of a sudden

384
00:29:29,664 --> 00:29:30,999
‎she went and…

385
00:29:32,417 --> 00:29:35,461
‎She hit me. She actually punched me.

386
00:29:35,545 --> 00:29:37,505
‎"You good-for-nothing brat,

387
00:29:37,589 --> 00:29:40,717
‎how dare you not visit me once
‎while I was alive?"

388
00:29:40,800 --> 00:29:43,344
‎"You don't deserve a good night's sleep!"

389
00:29:43,428 --> 00:29:45,471
‎She was exactly how I remember her.

390
00:29:45,555 --> 00:29:48,057
‎You know those old canes
‎that old people used?

391
00:29:48,141 --> 00:29:50,018
‎It hurt when she hit you, didn't it?

392
00:29:50,101 --> 00:29:51,895
‎Don't even ask. It hurt badly.

393
00:29:52,395 --> 00:29:53,563
‎Who are you?

394
00:30:02,113 --> 00:30:03,823
‎That wasn't a dream.

395
00:30:04,407 --> 00:30:05,700
‎Ms. Cheon?

396
00:30:09,037 --> 00:30:11,080
‎Cheon Yeo-ri.
‎It's Cheon Yeo-ri, the heiress.

397
00:30:11,164 --> 00:30:12,248
‎Mr. Ma.

398
00:30:13,750 --> 00:30:15,460
‎It's Prosecutor Ma Gang-uk.

399
00:30:15,543 --> 00:30:17,879
‎We shared a bed.

400
00:30:17,962 --> 00:30:19,464
‎You can't say that.

401
00:30:19,547 --> 00:30:21,424
‎-People could get the wrong idea.
‎-What?

402
00:30:22,967 --> 00:30:24,802
‎What brings you here? Where are the rest?

403
00:30:26,262 --> 00:30:27,972
‎I didn't bring anyone else.

404
00:30:28,056 --> 00:30:29,641
‎I'm here on my own.

405
00:30:29,724 --> 00:30:32,018
‎I didn't think you'd step foot
‎in places like this.

406
00:30:32,602 --> 00:30:34,228
‎They must know each other well.

407
00:30:34,312 --> 00:30:36,981
‎They don't just know each other.
‎I think they're best friends.

408
00:30:37,065 --> 00:30:39,567
‎We can't stand not getting answers.

409
00:30:39,651 --> 00:30:40,902
‎-Right.
‎-Hello. How are you?

410
00:30:40,985 --> 00:30:43,071
‎-Shall we?
‎-It's a pleasure to meet you.

411
00:30:43,571 --> 00:30:44,739
‎Stop.

412
00:30:47,033 --> 00:30:48,534
‎Maintain your distance.

413
00:30:49,327 --> 00:30:50,787
‎Take three steps back.

414
00:30:50,870 --> 00:30:52,538
‎Okay. Three steps back.

415
00:30:52,622 --> 00:30:54,248
‎One, two, three.

416
00:30:54,332 --> 00:30:55,667
‎-Sit down.
‎-Okay.

417
00:30:56,668 --> 00:30:59,128
‎I'm doing this for your sake, you know.

418
00:30:59,212 --> 00:31:01,881
‎I'm putting up a wall to keep you safe.

419
00:31:01,965 --> 00:31:03,925
‎If you make the mistake
‎of sitting with me,

420
00:31:04,425 --> 00:31:06,427
‎terrible things could happen to you.

421
00:31:07,303 --> 00:31:10,181
‎That's why I paid in advance

422
00:31:11,224 --> 00:31:13,935
‎to keep the tables around me empty.

423
00:31:14,018 --> 00:31:17,397
‎So no one can even come near me.

424
00:31:17,480 --> 00:31:19,482
‎I get that you want to flaunt your money,

425
00:31:19,565 --> 00:31:21,693
‎but why bother to come here
‎just to drink alone?

426
00:31:22,652 --> 00:31:23,486
‎"Why bother"?

427
00:31:24,487 --> 00:31:26,531
‎It's not the same.

428
00:31:26,614 --> 00:31:29,659
‎Here, if I look up from a drink,

429
00:31:29,742 --> 00:31:31,035
‎I see people.

430
00:31:31,119 --> 00:31:33,746
‎At home, if I look up from a drink…

431
00:31:40,878 --> 00:31:41,713
‎Forget it.

432
00:31:41,796 --> 00:31:45,508
‎-She emptied seven bottles of soju.
‎-She's out of it.

433
00:31:45,591 --> 00:31:48,511
‎Every now and then, I want to drink

434
00:31:48,594 --> 00:31:51,931
‎among some ordinary people.

435
00:32:02,650 --> 00:32:04,318
‎Wait…

436
00:32:04,402 --> 00:32:06,070
‎Do it properly then.

437
00:32:06,154 --> 00:32:07,947
‎-What?
‎-Come and join us.

438
00:32:08,031 --> 00:32:09,907
‎-Yes, sure.
‎-Shall we?

439
00:32:09,991 --> 00:32:11,409
‎No, you can't.

440
00:32:12,243 --> 00:32:14,245
‎-Go away. Leave.
‎-Excuse us.

441
00:32:14,328 --> 00:32:18,124
‎If you join me,
‎you might get a taste of the afterlife.

442
00:32:18,207 --> 00:32:19,876
‎If we do, then so be it.

443
00:32:20,460 --> 00:32:21,294
‎Here.

444
00:32:22,795 --> 00:32:23,838
‎Drink up.

445
00:32:26,883 --> 00:32:29,510
‎You filled my glass, so I should empty it.

446
00:32:33,514 --> 00:32:35,058
‎It's been so long

447
00:32:35,141 --> 00:32:37,602
‎since someone poured me a drink.

448
00:32:41,731 --> 00:32:43,983
‎-They must have a thing.
‎-They're playing hard to get.

449
00:32:44,067 --> 00:32:45,068
‎It's not like that.

450
00:32:45,985 --> 00:32:47,111
‎It's not.

451
00:32:50,698 --> 00:32:53,785
‎Earlier, when I was talking about
‎the dream of my grandma,

452
00:32:53,868 --> 00:32:55,661
‎what did you mean it wasn't a dream?

453
00:32:55,745 --> 00:32:57,622
‎Oh, that?

454
00:32:59,540 --> 00:33:00,917
‎You guys have no idea

455
00:33:01,667 --> 00:33:04,420
‎that the dead come visit you
‎while you sleep, do you?

456
00:33:06,005 --> 00:33:08,216
‎They come and watch you while you sleep.

457
00:33:09,300 --> 00:33:10,760
‎They just stare…

458
00:33:11,511 --> 00:33:12,345
‎like this.

459
00:33:12,929 --> 00:33:15,223
‎They sometimes give you sleep paralysis

460
00:33:15,973 --> 00:33:17,308
‎or even strangle you.

461
00:33:17,892 --> 00:33:20,895
‎People think they're just nightmares.

462
00:33:25,149 --> 00:33:26,651
‎You think they're all dreams, don't you?

463
00:33:31,280 --> 00:33:33,199
‎You would never know

464
00:33:33,282 --> 00:33:35,701
‎when you only ever see one side of things.

465
00:33:37,328 --> 00:33:39,205
‎You can't drink soju out of a bowl.

466
00:33:39,288 --> 00:33:40,456
‎That will kill you.

467
00:33:40,540 --> 00:33:42,708
‎What? Why would I die?

468
00:33:42,792 --> 00:33:46,546
‎No, I mean if you drink this much at once,

469
00:33:46,629 --> 00:33:48,297
‎it'll ruin your liver and your stomach.

470
00:33:48,381 --> 00:33:49,799
‎What if you were to fall ill?

471
00:33:49,882 --> 00:33:52,176
‎It'd be hard on you,
‎but also on your family.

472
00:33:52,260 --> 00:33:53,302
‎Shut up.

473
00:33:57,515 --> 00:34:00,476
‎You think my family would worry about me?

474
00:34:01,310 --> 00:34:02,145
‎What makes you say that?

475
00:34:03,354 --> 00:34:04,981
‎Do you even know me?

476
00:34:05,773 --> 00:34:08,693
‎What do you even know about me
‎to say something like that?

477
00:34:08,776 --> 00:34:12,029
‎What do people like you know

478
00:34:12,113 --> 00:34:14,490
‎when you're able to drink in a crowd?

479
00:34:14,574 --> 00:34:17,326
‎All you see with your two eyes
‎is the outer skin.

480
00:34:21,205 --> 00:34:22,039
‎Skin.

481
00:34:23,291 --> 00:34:24,625
‎This is a skin too.

482
00:34:25,501 --> 00:34:26,377
‎Skin.

483
00:34:29,922 --> 00:34:32,133
‎I don't need extra layers like these.

484
00:34:33,926 --> 00:34:36,846
‎Why'd you take off the gloves
‎you're always wearing?

485
00:34:45,855 --> 00:34:47,857
‎-In this pork skin diner…
‎-What?

486
00:34:48,649 --> 00:34:50,401
‎Eating these pork skin…

487
00:34:52,195 --> 00:34:54,739
‎Only seeing the skin that meets the eye…

488
00:34:54,822 --> 00:34:57,950
‎-Wait…
‎-You're just a skin-deep prosecutor!

489
00:35:03,414 --> 00:35:05,625
‎Skin-deep!

490
00:35:06,209 --> 00:35:07,126
‎What the…

491
00:35:08,920 --> 00:35:11,464
‎Skin-deep!

492
00:35:21,224 --> 00:35:22,225
‎You should…

493
00:35:24,685 --> 00:35:25,811
‎be stripped…

494
00:35:30,775 --> 00:35:33,110
‎of your skin!

495
00:36:10,314 --> 00:36:11,190
‎Pil-dong.

496
00:36:12,650 --> 00:36:13,818
‎Can you lend me a shirt?

497
00:36:15,361 --> 00:36:17,029
‎I think you'll have to go home like that.

498
00:36:46,934 --> 00:36:48,227
‎What is this?

499
00:36:49,812 --> 00:36:52,898
‎Man, never have I seen
‎such a drunken habit.

500
00:36:52,982 --> 00:36:56,861
‎I mean, forget that she was drunk,
‎but calling me "skin-deep"?

501
00:36:56,944 --> 00:37:00,781
‎And why should I know her?
‎I could say the same about her.

502
00:37:00,865 --> 00:37:04,702
‎Besides, why not drink on her own at home
‎instead of reserving half the diner?

503
00:37:04,785 --> 00:37:07,121
‎She calls herself the CEO of a hotel,

504
00:37:07,204 --> 00:37:09,206
‎yet she pulls
‎a drunken stunt like that in public?

505
00:37:09,874 --> 00:37:12,418
‎Man, it was a new shirt too.

506
00:37:12,918 --> 00:37:16,005
‎Can't you at least react
‎at the bare minimum?

507
00:37:16,589 --> 00:37:17,506
‎Hello?

508
00:37:19,133 --> 00:37:20,217
‎Did you say something?

509
00:37:21,802 --> 00:37:23,095
‎Oh, come on.

510
00:37:24,638 --> 00:37:26,098
‎I'm sick of you. Get out.

511
00:37:26,807 --> 00:37:29,852
‎You can't corner me like this
‎just because we're carpooling in your car.

512
00:37:29,935 --> 00:37:32,480
‎I'm not cornering you.
‎We're here, so get out.

513
00:37:33,939 --> 00:37:35,441
‎Oh, when did we get here?

514
00:37:43,366 --> 00:37:45,201
‎Hello? You go ahead.

515
00:37:45,284 --> 00:37:47,536
‎It's me, Cheon Yeo-ri.

516
00:37:47,620 --> 00:37:48,704
‎What do you want?

517
00:37:49,538 --> 00:37:50,998
‎Well, I think…

518
00:37:51,082 --> 00:37:54,210
‎I might have acted out of line last night.

519
00:37:54,293 --> 00:37:55,503
‎You mean ripping my shirt up?

520
00:37:56,670 --> 00:37:59,340
‎Don't worry about it.
‎It's fine. I threw it away.

521
00:37:59,840 --> 00:38:01,509
‎I'm not fine with what I did.

522
00:38:02,635 --> 00:38:05,304
‎I can't stand owing anyone anything.

523
00:38:06,972 --> 00:38:08,974
‎What did you send me?

524
00:38:15,815 --> 00:38:17,525
‎Yes, I knew it.

525
00:38:17,608 --> 00:38:18,943
‎It's Éthria.

526
00:38:21,278 --> 00:38:23,489
‎Look at this. It's pure silk.

527
00:38:23,572 --> 00:38:25,408
‎How much do these cost?

528
00:38:25,491 --> 00:38:27,827
‎This is a high-end luxury brand,

529
00:38:28,411 --> 00:38:29,453
‎so at least three million won?

530
00:38:29,537 --> 00:38:30,746
‎What?

531
00:38:30,830 --> 00:38:34,333
‎What's the nicest thing Ma can buy
‎without feeling guilty or tethered?

532
00:38:34,917 --> 00:38:35,960
‎Pork belly.

533
00:38:36,460 --> 00:38:37,920
‎What's the nicest thing he can accept?

534
00:38:38,754 --> 00:38:40,172
‎Two cups of iced coffee?

535
00:38:41,215 --> 00:38:43,926
‎That won't do. In that case,

536
00:38:44,009 --> 00:38:45,386
‎I'll carry it very safely…

537
00:38:45,469 --> 00:38:48,139
‎-Why would you take it?
‎-I should.

538
00:38:48,222 --> 00:38:50,558
‎Silk shirts look better on me.

539
00:38:50,641 --> 00:38:52,601
‎-You can't handle them.
‎-That's what you think.

540
00:38:52,685 --> 00:38:54,103
‎You really can't handle a silk shirt.

541
00:38:54,186 --> 00:38:56,814
‎-You don't know--
‎-Éthria goods are…

542
00:38:56,897 --> 00:38:58,149
‎What? Mr. Ma.

543
00:38:59,275 --> 00:39:01,193
‎That Éthria shirt…

544
00:39:14,039 --> 00:39:15,416
‎Hello, good morning.

545
00:39:15,499 --> 00:39:17,460
‎I'm here to see Ms. Cheon.

546
00:39:17,543 --> 00:39:19,253
‎-Oh, Ms. Cheon?
‎-Yes.

547
00:39:19,336 --> 00:39:21,297
‎-Please give me a moment.
‎-Sure.

548
00:39:25,217 --> 00:39:26,594
‎-Hello.
‎-Yes, hi.

549
00:39:26,677 --> 00:39:28,929
‎The hotel gym and sauna, right?

550
00:39:32,057 --> 00:39:34,935
‎I'm Ms. Cheon's executive secretary.
‎Ms. Cheon isn't in at the moment.

551
00:39:37,188 --> 00:39:39,064
‎She sent this to me today.

552
00:39:39,565 --> 00:39:40,858
‎If you're her secretary,
‎pass it to her for me.

553
00:39:40,941 --> 00:39:43,360
‎-No, I can't do that.
‎-Why not?

554
00:39:43,444 --> 00:39:44,820
‎If Ms. Cheon sent it to you herself,

555
00:39:44,904 --> 00:39:46,864
‎we're not allowed to
‎take it back on her behalf.

556
00:39:47,990 --> 00:39:50,493
‎What else am I supposed to do with it?

557
00:39:50,576 --> 00:39:53,120
‎Could you return it yourself,
‎if you don't mind?

558
00:39:55,623 --> 00:39:56,457
‎Jeez…

559
00:40:00,794 --> 00:40:01,629
‎Ms. Eom?

560
00:40:03,130 --> 00:40:06,884
‎Wasn't the man who came to see
‎Ms. Cheon here before?

561
00:40:06,967 --> 00:40:08,844
‎He was. This was his second visit.

562
00:40:09,887 --> 00:40:12,223
‎Could he be a stalker following Ms. Cheon?

563
00:40:12,306 --> 00:40:14,350
‎No, he's a Seoul
‎Central District prosecutor.

564
00:40:15,351 --> 00:40:17,436
‎Could he be pretending to be a prosecutor?

565
00:40:17,520 --> 00:40:18,395
‎I doubt that.

566
00:40:18,979 --> 00:40:22,733
‎His office once sent a questionnaire
‎to our legal team.

567
00:40:22,816 --> 00:40:24,443
‎Oh, right.

568
00:40:24,527 --> 00:40:26,362
‎Do you know why
‎he wanted to see Ms. Cheon?

569
00:40:27,947 --> 00:40:30,324
‎It seems that Ms. Cheon sent him a gift

570
00:40:30,407 --> 00:40:31,700
‎and he wanted to return it.

571
00:40:32,743 --> 00:40:34,411
‎That's a problem.

572
00:40:35,079 --> 00:40:37,206
‎Whether it be from an official
‎or a private standpoint,

573
00:40:37,289 --> 00:40:40,793
‎it's a problem if she sent a gift
‎to a Central District prosecutor.

574
00:40:40,876 --> 00:40:44,213
‎Shouldn't we call a meeting
‎for damage control and countermeasures?

575
00:40:44,296 --> 00:40:48,050
‎If there is a problem,
‎I'm sure Ms. Cheon will handle it.

576
00:40:48,676 --> 00:40:49,593
‎No, no.

577
00:40:50,177 --> 00:40:52,930
‎We need to take action. My hunch says so.

578
00:40:53,597 --> 00:40:54,640
‎It's never wrong.

579
00:40:55,516 --> 00:40:56,600
‎Yes.

580
00:40:57,101 --> 00:40:58,185
‎That's my coffee.

581
00:40:58,727 --> 00:40:59,853
‎Oh, I was wrong.

582
00:41:01,814 --> 00:41:02,648
‎Wrong.

583
00:41:12,199 --> 00:41:15,995
‎It's not that big a favor.
‎Why couldn't she just return it for me?

584
00:41:16,078 --> 00:41:17,079
‎Jeez.

585
00:41:17,162 --> 00:41:18,789
‎Why does she live so far away?

586
00:41:33,345 --> 00:41:35,306
‎No wonder she reserved half the diner.

587
00:41:36,265 --> 00:41:37,891
‎Where did they go?

588
00:41:38,684 --> 00:41:40,060
‎They're the only thing that's missing.

589
00:41:41,478 --> 00:41:42,980
‎Where did I take them off?

590
00:41:46,984 --> 00:41:47,901
‎Who could that be?

591
00:41:48,527 --> 00:41:49,862
‎I didn't order any delivery.

592
00:41:56,577 --> 00:41:57,870
‎It's him again.

593
00:41:59,455 --> 00:42:00,581
‎What's he doing here?

594
00:42:04,335 --> 00:42:06,045
‎How did you find me?

595
00:42:06,128 --> 00:42:07,588
‎I put your address in my GPS.

596
00:42:08,631 --> 00:42:09,757
‎The GPS?

597
00:42:09,840 --> 00:42:12,134
‎How did you get my address?

598
00:42:13,344 --> 00:42:14,261
‎Don't you remember?

599
00:42:14,928 --> 00:42:15,971
‎You gave it to me.

600
00:42:16,055 --> 00:42:17,139
‎I did?

601
00:42:18,390 --> 00:42:19,433
‎I wouldn't…

602
00:42:38,077 --> 00:42:38,911
‎Hey.

603
00:42:39,578 --> 00:42:41,622
‎Hello? Your address.

604
00:42:41,705 --> 00:42:43,082
‎Tell me your address.

605
00:42:43,165 --> 00:42:44,083
‎My address?

606
00:42:44,750 --> 00:42:48,337
‎-My address is Seongbuk-gu, Seoul…
‎-What?

607
00:42:50,923 --> 00:42:51,757
‎Okay.

608
00:42:52,257 --> 00:42:54,051
‎Can you put this into the GPS?

609
00:42:58,972 --> 00:43:00,808
‎I'm really sorry.

610
00:43:00,891 --> 00:43:03,394
‎I was in the middle of something…

611
00:43:03,477 --> 00:43:04,395
‎Never mind that.

612
00:43:05,521 --> 00:43:07,147
‎I just came here to return this.

613
00:43:07,231 --> 00:43:09,650
‎I'm not able to come out right now.

614
00:43:10,401 --> 00:43:12,820
‎Could you leave it by the gate?

615
00:43:13,445 --> 00:43:14,822
‎Sure. I'll do that.

616
00:43:19,952 --> 00:43:21,870
‎I'll leave these here as well.

617
00:43:22,830 --> 00:43:24,164
‎You left them at the diner.

618
00:43:25,457 --> 00:43:26,291
‎What?

619
00:43:26,792 --> 00:43:27,960
‎Why does he have my gloves?

620
00:43:36,385 --> 00:43:38,262
‎I don't need extra layers like these.

621
00:43:40,556 --> 00:43:43,183
‎You should be stripped

622
00:43:43,267 --> 00:43:44,101
‎of your skin!

623
00:43:51,150 --> 00:43:52,276
‎Hey, you forgot your gloves.

624
00:44:10,127 --> 00:44:10,961
‎Oh, no.

625
00:44:14,173 --> 00:44:15,674
‎I must've been out of my mind.

626
00:44:16,800 --> 00:44:18,802
‎I'll leave both of these together

627
00:44:18,886 --> 00:44:21,472
‎-by the gate here.
‎-I did that without my gloves?

628
00:44:23,974 --> 00:44:26,769
‎That's why I couldn't find them anywhere.

629
00:44:26,852 --> 00:44:28,729
‎-What now?
‎-I've left them here.

630
00:44:30,564 --> 00:44:31,398
‎I'm leaving now.

631
00:44:33,901 --> 00:44:34,985
‎Should I ask?

632
00:44:36,278 --> 00:44:38,071
‎Wait. Wait.

633
00:44:38,155 --> 00:44:38,989
‎What?

634
00:44:45,746 --> 00:44:48,123
‎What? Does she want me to come in?

635
00:45:17,361 --> 00:45:19,821
‎Your house is really quiet.

636
00:45:21,240 --> 00:45:22,282
‎Yes.

637
00:45:25,827 --> 00:45:26,745
‎Look, Mr. Ma.

638
00:45:28,539 --> 00:45:31,208
‎By any chance, every now and then,

639
00:45:31,708 --> 00:45:34,836
‎do you happen to see things
‎you weren't able to before?

640
00:45:38,006 --> 00:45:40,342
‎There's a tent in your living room.

641
00:45:40,926 --> 00:45:42,594
‎Yes, well…

642
00:45:42,678 --> 00:45:45,138
‎It's pretty cozy inside.

643
00:45:45,222 --> 00:45:49,017
‎As you can see,
‎this house is too big for me alone.

644
00:45:50,352 --> 00:45:51,687
‎It really is quite big.

645
00:45:51,770 --> 00:45:54,982
‎My parents used to live with me,
‎though not anymore.

646
00:45:58,026 --> 00:45:59,194
‎-Try the tea.
‎-Thanks.

647
00:46:08,036 --> 00:46:09,746
‎Why did you want me to come in?

648
00:46:09,830 --> 00:46:11,790
‎You don't seem the type to have guests.

649
00:46:12,833 --> 00:46:15,711
‎Well, you came all this way,

650
00:46:15,794 --> 00:46:18,338
‎so it felt wrong
‎to just send you on your way.

651
00:46:18,422 --> 00:46:20,173
‎And I wanted to check something too.

652
00:46:20,257 --> 00:46:22,301
‎Check what? With me?

653
00:46:23,260 --> 00:46:24,595
‎So last night…

654
00:46:25,387 --> 00:46:27,556
‎I was a bit out of line.

655
00:46:28,223 --> 00:46:30,851
‎I touched you without my gloves…

656
00:46:36,231 --> 00:46:37,399
‎Who's that kid?

657
00:46:45,699 --> 00:46:47,075
‎Who is that?

658
00:46:55,584 --> 00:46:58,045
‎-He's from next door.
‎-What's he doing here?

659
00:47:00,380 --> 00:47:01,423
‎Playing hide and seek.

660
00:47:01,506 --> 00:47:03,592
‎He comes here sometimes to play.

661
00:47:03,675 --> 00:47:05,302
‎Oh, really?

662
00:47:06,219 --> 00:47:07,346
‎He must be bored.

663
00:47:07,888 --> 00:47:09,848
‎If it's because his parents aren't home,

664
00:47:09,931 --> 00:47:11,600
‎-I'll play with him for a bit.
‎-No.

665
00:47:12,309 --> 00:47:13,310
‎You can't do that.

666
00:47:13,810 --> 00:47:14,853
‎You can't do anything.

667
00:47:14,936 --> 00:47:16,855
‎I'm really good with kids.

668
00:47:18,690 --> 00:47:21,109
‎You were here to return these, right?

669
00:47:21,193 --> 00:47:23,028
‎You returned them and I received them.

670
00:47:23,111 --> 00:47:24,154
‎All is well.

671
00:47:24,237 --> 00:47:26,281
‎You can leave now.

672
00:47:26,782 --> 00:47:27,824
‎Go on your way.

673
00:47:28,408 --> 00:47:29,242
‎Goodbye.

674
00:47:32,079 --> 00:47:33,747
‎-What was that?
‎-The wind.

675
00:47:35,582 --> 00:47:38,126
‎The doors are closed.
‎It couldn't have been the wind.

676
00:47:39,461 --> 00:47:41,463
‎Could it be a burglar?

677
00:47:42,005 --> 00:47:42,839
‎What?

678
00:47:42,923 --> 00:47:44,925
‎They could've scaled the wall
‎to hide somewhere.

679
00:47:45,008 --> 00:47:46,760
‎I worked on a case like that.

680
00:47:46,843 --> 00:47:49,388
‎Listen. I have a security system,

681
00:47:49,471 --> 00:47:50,972
‎so that would be impossible.

682
00:47:51,056 --> 00:47:51,890
‎Wait.

683
00:47:52,474 --> 00:47:53,809
‎I could just be paranoid,

684
00:47:53,892 --> 00:47:56,436
‎but it doesn't hurt to check,
‎and it won't take that long.

685
00:47:57,312 --> 00:47:58,146
‎No.

686
00:47:58,814 --> 00:47:59,773
‎It's not a burglar.

687
00:48:01,692 --> 00:48:03,735
‎It must've been the kid.

688
00:48:03,819 --> 00:48:06,530
‎You see, there's an open door in the back.

689
00:48:06,613 --> 00:48:07,614
‎There is?

690
00:48:08,407 --> 00:48:10,200
‎Goodness, what a sneaky kid.

691
00:48:11,368 --> 00:48:12,494
‎Wait. Mr. Ma.

692
00:48:12,994 --> 00:48:14,371
‎It's fine. It won't take long.

693
00:48:14,454 --> 00:48:16,289
‎-I told you to go.
‎-Just wait.

694
00:48:17,666 --> 00:48:19,126
‎Are you in here?

695
00:48:19,209 --> 00:48:20,127
‎What?

696
00:48:20,210 --> 00:48:21,294
‎You're not in here.

697
00:48:21,962 --> 00:48:23,839
‎I'd better get going then.

698
00:48:23,922 --> 00:48:26,341
‎Ms. Cheon, you'll come with me, right?

699
00:48:27,092 --> 00:48:27,968
‎Where?

700
00:48:29,845 --> 00:48:31,763
‎-Come here.
‎-What are you…

701
00:48:32,472 --> 00:48:35,225
‎What are you doing?
‎How did you know this was a door?

702
00:48:35,308 --> 00:48:36,810
‎What are you…

703
00:48:51,658 --> 00:48:53,368
‎That must be him coming out.

704
00:48:54,661 --> 00:48:55,579
‎Who do you mean?

705
00:49:11,094 --> 00:49:12,721
‎Did you see that?

706
00:49:12,804 --> 00:49:14,014
‎He moved so fast.

707
00:49:14,097 --> 00:49:16,850
‎Gosh, it was like… He almost…

708
00:49:16,933 --> 00:49:17,768
‎That was…

709
00:49:18,268 --> 00:49:19,144
‎Excuse me.

710
00:49:19,227 --> 00:49:20,479
‎Yes?

711
00:49:21,062 --> 00:49:23,190
‎I'm really tired.

712
00:49:24,858 --> 00:49:25,692
‎Please leave.

713
00:49:27,778 --> 00:49:30,197
‎I was too dull-witted to catch on.

714
00:49:30,989 --> 00:49:32,032
‎I'm sorry.

715
00:49:43,126 --> 00:49:43,960
‎My coat.

716
00:49:52,594 --> 00:49:53,845
‎What should I do now?

717
00:49:55,096 --> 00:49:56,306
‎What do I do now?

718
00:50:18,370 --> 00:50:19,371
‎Will he be okay?

719
00:50:25,627 --> 00:50:26,920
‎What should I do?

720
00:50:56,825 --> 00:50:58,952
‎What are you doing over there, kid?

721
00:50:59,035 --> 00:51:00,745
‎Shouldn't you be going home?

722
00:51:01,580 --> 00:51:03,456
‎Library hours are over now.

723
00:51:06,167 --> 00:51:08,545
‎I can't go home.

724
00:51:30,483 --> 00:51:31,526
‎That hurt.

725
00:51:41,828 --> 00:51:42,662
‎I must be

726
00:51:43,622 --> 00:51:44,539
‎way too on edge.

727
00:52:12,943 --> 00:52:15,070
‎Why the hell won't this open?

728
00:52:20,742 --> 00:52:22,494
‎-Hello?
‎-Hello?

729
00:52:23,578 --> 00:52:24,829
‎He's in my home right now.

730
00:52:26,206 --> 00:52:28,458
‎-Who?
‎-The kid who was playing hide and seek.

731
00:52:32,295 --> 00:52:33,546
‎-The little boy?
‎-Yes.

732
00:52:33,630 --> 00:52:35,006
‎He came all the way to my home.

733
00:52:51,564 --> 00:52:52,565
‎Mr. Ma?

734
00:52:53,400 --> 00:52:54,234
‎I'm here.

735
00:52:54,734 --> 00:52:55,694
‎Over here.

736
00:52:58,822 --> 00:53:00,532
‎Were you out here this whole time?

737
00:53:04,452 --> 00:53:05,286
‎Sit down here with me.

738
00:53:06,496 --> 00:53:07,706
‎What…

739
00:53:09,165 --> 00:53:11,543
‎Who is that kid? He climbs walls too.

740
00:53:24,597 --> 00:53:26,391
‎SOJU

741
00:53:27,058 --> 00:53:28,560
‎You carry this stuff around with you?

742
00:53:28,643 --> 00:53:31,813
‎It's a bag I keep handy
‎in case of emergencies.

743
00:53:32,355 --> 00:53:33,732
‎Try to calm down.

744
00:53:34,941 --> 00:53:35,859
‎Drink that first.

745
00:53:49,539 --> 00:53:52,167
‎Do you feel a bit relaxed now?

746
00:53:53,918 --> 00:53:55,003
‎What do you mean "relaxed"?

747
00:53:55,086 --> 00:53:57,964
‎Are you going to say something
‎that'll shock me?

748
00:54:00,425 --> 00:54:03,553
‎I have what it takes.
‎You can say whatever it is.

749
00:54:08,058 --> 00:54:09,059
‎Go on.

750
00:54:09,142 --> 00:54:10,060
‎Are you sure?

751
00:54:20,528 --> 00:54:21,446
‎No way.

752
00:54:40,215 --> 00:54:41,883
‎You weren't relaxed enough.

753
00:54:41,966 --> 00:54:44,594
‎Here. You need to stay with me.

754
00:54:45,136 --> 00:54:47,430
‎Have a few more sips of alcohol.

755
00:54:47,514 --> 00:54:49,349
‎Gulp it down. Don't spit it out.

756
00:54:56,106 --> 00:54:57,982
‎-He's not here.
‎-Okay.

757
00:55:01,111 --> 00:55:03,113
‎How did you know the body was there?

758
00:55:03,947 --> 00:55:05,448
‎-I was told.
‎-By whom?

759
00:55:06,783 --> 00:55:07,909
‎By a ghost.

760
00:55:09,244 --> 00:55:10,662
‎So she was telling the truth.

761
00:55:17,001 --> 00:55:18,169
‎Should I just turn the lights on?

762
00:55:19,087 --> 00:55:20,421
‎He doesn't like bright lights.

763
00:55:22,549 --> 00:55:24,008
‎You're sticking too close to me.

764
00:55:24,092 --> 00:55:26,010
‎I'm not standing that close.

765
00:55:26,094 --> 00:55:27,554
‎Wait outside if you're scared.

766
00:55:27,637 --> 00:55:30,348
‎I'm not scared, I'm just nervous.

767
00:55:34,144 --> 00:55:36,646
‎-Do you live alone too?
‎-Yes.

768
00:55:38,356 --> 00:55:41,609
‎Your place feels comfortable and cozy.

769
00:55:42,318 --> 00:55:46,030
‎I owe that to my grandma.
‎She sweeps and cleans whenever she visits.

770
00:55:46,531 --> 00:55:48,658
‎Huh? Wait…

771
00:55:51,077 --> 00:55:52,912
‎Does the kid like cars?

772
00:56:04,883 --> 00:56:06,551
‎He's a kid, so he'll be hiding.

773
00:56:10,180 --> 00:56:11,389
‎You must be good with housework.

774
00:56:11,973 --> 00:56:14,726
‎Yes. I'm good at everything I do.

775
00:56:37,040 --> 00:56:38,208
‎Oh, this is just…

776
00:56:39,042 --> 00:56:41,211
‎I always check out of habit.

777
00:56:41,294 --> 00:56:42,462
‎It's a work-related habit.

778
00:56:50,386 --> 00:56:52,222
‎Do you think he could've left?

779
00:56:54,641 --> 00:56:55,850
‎That's strange.

780
00:56:56,434 --> 00:56:59,020
‎Kids rarely leave
‎once they latch onto you.

781
00:57:00,521 --> 00:57:02,065
‎Where do they stay if they don't go?

782
00:57:04,984 --> 00:57:06,569
‎Why? What is it?

783
00:57:07,779 --> 00:57:08,988
‎Kids tend to…

784
00:57:09,072 --> 00:57:10,156
‎Yes?

785
00:57:12,575 --> 00:57:13,785
‎Piggyback on people.

786
00:57:28,633 --> 00:57:29,467
‎Get off me!

787
00:57:30,426 --> 00:57:32,679
‎-Mr. Ma! Keep still!
‎-Get off me!

788
00:57:32,762 --> 00:57:34,222
‎Go away!

789
00:57:35,390 --> 00:57:36,474
‎You said you weren't scared!

790
00:57:38,017 --> 00:57:40,144
‎No! No!

791
00:57:40,228 --> 00:57:41,312
‎Go away!

792
00:57:43,523 --> 00:57:45,275
‎He's off your back now!

793
00:57:45,358 --> 00:57:47,235
‎He's gone!

794
00:57:48,194 --> 00:57:49,654
‎He's gone!

795
00:57:50,154 --> 00:57:51,155
‎He's gone?

796
00:57:51,656 --> 00:57:52,574
‎He's gone?

797
00:58:45,960 --> 00:58:48,338
‎SPOOKY IN LOVE

798
00:58:48,421 --> 00:58:50,089
‎What do we do now?

799
00:58:50,173 --> 00:58:51,924
‎More ghosts will come for you.

800
00:58:53,885 --> 00:58:56,888
‎What happened to the other people
‎you came in contact with?

801
00:58:56,971 --> 00:58:59,223
‎The ghosts that visit you early on

802
00:58:59,307 --> 00:59:02,727
‎will be the nasty ones
‎that harass and torment others.

803
00:59:02,810 --> 00:59:04,062
‎You believe in all this?

804
00:59:04,145 --> 00:59:06,606
‎-There must be something about ghosts.
‎-Look.

805
00:59:06,689 --> 00:59:08,816
‎Look at him stuffing his face
‎with all that garlic.

806
00:59:08,900 --> 00:59:10,360
‎What's gotten into him?

807
00:59:10,443 --> 00:59:11,486
‎You swore on your life

808
00:59:11,569 --> 00:59:14,781
‎that you'd help me take over Reina
‎once you get out of here.

809
00:59:15,365 --> 00:59:16,199
‎Did you mean that?

810
00:59:17,158 --> 00:59:18,201
‎You bet I did.

811
00:59:19,035 --> 00:59:21,704
‎It makes no sense that a murderer like him
‎is getting released!

812
00:59:21,788 --> 00:59:23,206
‎Park Seung-jae.

813
00:59:23,289 --> 00:59:27,085
‎I plan to find a weakness
‎instead of going after you,

814
00:59:27,168 --> 00:59:28,169
‎Cheon Yeo-ri.

815
00:59:28,920 --> 00:59:33,925
‎Subtitle translation by: Jennifer Jean Lim

